# Quality and deployment

## Tests

Every API-contract fix has a regression test. Cover at least:

- SSE chunks split at arbitrary byte boundaries
- CRLF event separators
- structured `sources[]` objects (not URL strings)
- `success: false` application errors
- `insufficient` and `conflicting` evidence
- `no_match_found`
- scheduled vs finished
- empty `highlights[]`
- non-match intents
- abort behavior where practical

`npm run lint`, tests, and `npm run build` must pass before declaring SHIP.

Do not weaken TypeScript `strict` to make a build pass. Do not add `eslint-disable` or type assertions as a shortcut unless locally justified.

## Production configuration

One frontend API configuration boundary. Normalize the base URL and strip a trailing slash there.

- Local development may default to `http://localhost:8000`.
- Production must require `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://YOUR_VPS_API_HOST`.
- Do not silently fall back to localhost in a production browser.
- Production API traffic must use HTTPS.

Document `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` and backend `CORS_ORIGINS`. The VPS backend must list the deployed frontend origin.

Retain `request_id` / `X-Request-ID` for debugging.

Do not commit secrets or `.env.local`. `.env.example` may contain only public frontend configuration.
